@startuml
title Deployment Diagram - TravelWise (current, as-run state)

node "Developer Machine (Windows)" {
  node "Node.js runtime" {
    component "Vite dev server\n(client)\n:5173" as Vite
    component "Express API\n(server)\n:5000" as Express
  }
  node "Python 3.13 venv" {
    component "Flask ML service\n(ml-service)\n:8000" as Flask
    artifact "model.joblib"
  }
}

cloud "Supabase Cloud" {
  database "PostgreSQL" as PG
  component "Auth service" as Auth
}

Vite --> Express : HTTP (proxied /api)
Express --> Flask : HTTP :8000
Express --> PG : REST (service role key)
Vite --> Auth : REST (publishable key)

note bottom
  This reflects the system as it actually runs
  today (local dev, three local processes + a
  managed cloud database). The target three-host
  cloud deployment described in Assignment 2
  (React on Vercel; Node + Python on Render) has
  NOT been carried out — see Limitations (5.4)
  and the traceability matrix (2.2) for the
  deployment-related requirement's honest status.
end note

@enduml
